----------------\n### 5.  Impossibility of other values of \\(k\\)\n\nThe only restriction on \\(k\\) is the trivial bound \\(k\\le n\\) (there are only \\(n\\) lines).  \nThe construction above shows that every integer \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n\\) is attainable.  \nHence no other non\u2011negative integer can occur.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 6.  Conclusion\n\nFor any integer \\(n\\ge 3\\) the set of admissible numbers of sunny lines is exactly  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\{0,1,2,\\dots ,n\\}} .\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------"
