added non\u2011sunny vertical\nlines provided \\(a\\ge 2\\)) covers the point; similarly for the case \\(b\\ge 2\\)\nwith a horizontal line.  Hence every lattice point of \\(T_n\\) lies on at least\none of the constructed lines.\n\nThe construction uses exactly two non\u2011sunny axis\u2011parallel lines, the \\(k\\)\nsunny lines, and \\(n-2-k\\) further non\u2011sunny lines, for a total of \\(n\\) lines.\nConsequently the number of sunny lines is precisely \\(k\\).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 4.  Conclusion\n\nFrom (1) we have the necessary condition \\(k\\le n-2\\).  \nThe explicit constructions of Sections\u202f2 and\u202f3 show that for every integer\n\\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n-2\\) there exists a set of \\(n\\) distinct lines satisfying\nthe covering requirement and containing exactly \\(k\\) sunny lines.\n\nTherefore the complete set of admissible values of \\(k\\) is  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\;k\\in\\{0,1,2,\\dots ,n-2\\}\\; } .\n\\]"
