ism with an existing sunny line, all inserted lines are distinct and sunny.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n#### 2.3  Completion of the construction\n\nStarting from the base configuration (\\(k=0\\)), apply the pivot operation successively to obtain configurations with \\(k=1,2,\\dots ,n\\) sunny lines.  \nAt each step the total number of lines stays equal to \\(n\\) and the covering condition is preserved.  \nThus for every integer \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n\\) there exists a family of \\(n\\) distinct lines satisfying the two requirements and containing exactly \\(k\\) sunny lines.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 3.  Conclusion\n\nWe have proved:\n\n* No configuration can have more than \\(n\\) sunny lines (Section 1).\n* For each \\(k\\in\\{0,1,\\dots ,n\\}\\) a configuration with exactly \\(k\\) sunny lines exists (Section 2).\n\nHence the set of admissible values of \\(k\\) is precisely \\(\\{0,1,\\dots ,n\\}\\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{All integers }k\\text{ with }0\\le k\\le n\\text{ are possible}.}\n\\]"
